==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|svána}}. Composed of {{affix|is|svo|t1=so, thus|-na|pos2=proximal suffix}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsvɔːna/}}
* {{IPA|is|/ˈsɔːna/|a=colloquial}}
* {{rhymes|is|ɔːna|s=2}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv|-}}

# [[thus]], [[like this]]
#: {{ux|is|Til þess að hitta í körfuna verðurðu að kasta boltanum '''svona'''.|To hit the basket you have to throw the ball '''like this'''.}}
# to this degree; [[this]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég vissi ekki að þú værir '''svona''' góður!|I didn’t know you were '''this''' good!}}
# {{lb|is|colloquial}} [[approximately]], [[about]], [[like]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég fór síðast í bíó fyrir '''svona''' mánuði.|The last time I went to the movies was '''like''' a month ago.}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|like this}} {{l|is|þannig||like that}}, {{l|is|svoleiðis||like that}}
* {{sense|to this degree}} {{l|is|svo||so, to such a degree}}, {{l|is|það||to that degree}}

===Adjective===
{{is-adj|-}}

# [[like this]], [[such]]
#: {{ux|is|Það er eitthvað að '''svona''' fólki.|There’s something wrong with people '''like this'''.}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|like this}} {{l|is|slíkur||such, like that}}, {{l|is|þannig||like that}}, {{l|is|svoleiðis||like that}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|svona, svona||there, there}}

